1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,600
Hi, I'm Oladapo Olaniyan. This is my PepsiCo research evaluation

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:09,200
review. My current recommendation is watch and defer, rather than

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:12,800
buy now. The goal of this work was to rebuild

4
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:16,400
the valuation using more current financial information and then decide

5
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:20,000
whether the evidence supports buying at the market price.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,700
For Edition B, I used PepsiCo's 2025 fiscal year filing

7
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:29,400
and the latest interim bridge in my model. One important

8
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:34,100
correction involved capital spending. Consolidated capex is 4.415 billion dollars

9
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:38,800
and includes 4.192 billion from the segments and 223 million

10
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:43,500
of corporate capex. This correction matters because capital spending is

11
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:48,200
cash the company must invest to keep operating and growing.

12
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:52,900
If I use only the segment figure, I would understate

13
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:57,600
PepsiCo's total investment and overstate the cash that is available

14
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:02,300
to investors. That would make the valuation look stronger than

15
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:07,000
it should.

16
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:10,833
AI helped organize sources, build the model code, and prepare

17
00:01:10,833 --> 00:01:14,666
documentation. I recorded that use and checked key values against

18
00:01:14,666 --> 00:01:18,500
primary source arithmetic. I also ran validation checks to make

19
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:22,333
sure the forecast statements, cash flow and valuation bridge work

20
00:01:22,333 --> 00:01:26,166
together. Those checks confirm the model calculations run as intended.

21
00:01:26,166 --> 00:01:30,000
They do not prove that every financial assumption is correct.

22
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,857
For the changed input test, I lowered terminal ROIC, or

23
00:01:33,857 --> 00:01:37,714
return on capital investment, from 15 to 12 percent. A

24
00:01:37,714 --> 00:01:41,571
lower ROIC means more of the company's future profits will

25
00:01:41,571 --> 00:01:45,428
be reinstated and reinvested to support the same growth. The

26
00:01:45,428 --> 00:01:49,285
estimated value per share fell from 117.29 to 111.41, a

27
00:01:49,285 --> 00:01:53,142
5.88 dollar decline. This matched my recorded prediction and shows

28
00:01:53,142 --> 00:01:57,000
that the valuation is sensitive to long-run performance ability assumptions.

29
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,184
Overall, I recommend watch and defer. The remaining issues are

30
00:02:00,184 --> 00:02:03,368
the current date bridge, peer comparability, working capital reconciliation and

31
00:02:03,368 --> 00:02:06,552
final student judgment. I'll monitor revenue growth, operating margins, cash

32
00:02:06,552 --> 00:02:09,736
conversion and debt after future releases. Until those uncertainties are

33
00:02:09,736 --> 00:02:12,921
better supported, I'll monitor PepsiCo rather than recommending an immediate

34
00:02:12,921 --> 00:02:16,105
purchase.
